  "body": "Beach days at beautiful Campbells Bay, one of the North Shore best beaches, and dinner at El Greco - both within a five-minute walk. Add long lunches at home, and you've got summer sorted. Tucked off the end of a cul-de-sac, this private Campbells Bay home is ready for a summer well spent.\r\n\r\nTriple high school zoning means the school years are covered too. With Rangitoto College, Westlake Boys and Westlake Girls in the mix, this is a home your family can settle into and grow into.\r\n\r\nFollow the palms beneath the curved canopy and step inside. With 2.7 m ceilings, tall doors and fresh paint inside and out, there and an immediate feeling of light and space. Everything is on one level, making everyday family life easy.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen and dining sit between the family room and a separate lounge. Get everyone together for dinner, then spread out for the evening. There are four bedrooms, including a main bedroom with an ensuite, new double wardrobes and its own secluded deck. Take your first coffee out there before the rest of the house wakes up. The fourth bedroom works nicely as a home office.\r\n\r\nThrow open the bifolds and double doors on the north side and let summer fill the house. The family room opens straight onto a covered patio framed by palms and ferns. Fire up the barbecue, pull up a few extra chairs and settle in. There and a sunny lawn for the kids, a proper vege garden and a private garden path for a quiet wander at the end of the day. A previous owner removed the pool, but if a pool is on your wishlist, there and room to explore adding one again, subject to site suitability and any required approvals.\r\n\r\nThere is a workshop and wine cellar off the garage, while the double carport and generous off-street parking leave room for the weekend gear. Bring the boat. Bring the caravan, too.\r\n\r\nWhy you will love it\r\n- Triple high school zoning for Rangitoto College, Westlake Boys and Westlake Girls\r\n- Campbells Bay Beach and El Greco within a five-minute walk\r\n- 1,123 sqm of freehold land (more or less), tucked off the end of the cul-de-sac\r\n- Single-level living with four bedrooms, two bathrooms and two living areas\r\n- 2.7 m ceilings, tall doors and fresh paint inside and out\r\n- Main bedroom with ensuite, new double wardrobes and its own secluded deck\r\n- North-facing bifolds and double doors opening to covered entertaining\r\n- Sunny lawn, established vege garden and a private garden path\r\n- Potential to add a pool again, subject to site suitability and any required approvals\r\n- Double carport, garage, workshop, wine cellar and generous off-street parking\r\n\r\nMove in, unpack and get the barbecue going. Give Drew or Harrison a call and come see where you could spend your summer.\r\n\r\nAUCTION: Thursday 3rd December 2026 from 5pm at Ray White Milford (Unless Sold Prior)\r\nINFO: rwmairangibay.co.nz/MRG32534 (scroll down to documents)",
